-# reed — CC hooks & `claude agents --json` exploration log
-
-Empirical evidence for how the **reed** module (`internal/reedengine` — see the package documentation and [overview.md#modules](../overview.md#modules)) can drive tmux pane **switching/focus** off Claude Code's *own* signals — its **hook system** and the **`claude agents --json`** registry — rather than (or alongside) the `lyx reed spawn` replace-dispatch model.
-Companion to [`reed-exploration.md`](reed-exploration.md) (which proved the tmux primitives);
-this file proves the **CC-side** primitives.
-
-All claims below are hands-on, verified on this box unless marked **UNVERIFIED**.
-Probe scaffolding lived in `.scratch/hook-probe/` (gitignored): a `logger.ps1` that dumps each hook's raw stdin payload to a uniquely-named file, a `settings.json` wiring nine hook events to it,
-and an isolated tmux server (via tmux on Windows) running a **real interactive** `claude` — never `claude -p` (headless is out of scope;
-panes must be interactive sessions).
-
-Environment (verified 2026-06-15):
-- claude **2.1.177** (native, resolved via PATH)
-- tmux **3.3.4** (via tmux on Windows);
-  pwsh **7.6.2**
-- Probe model resolved to `claude-opus-4-8[1m]` (the box default).
